n  vaccination of non-human primates  with a molecule that maintains this  pre-fusion  state  so we sought to collaborate with the  inventors of this molecule which is  called  ds cap1 in order to introduce digesting  bonds  into a similar background in order to  generate a more potent and stable  molecule  as it would have manufacturing  advantages and also potentially more  potency  the influenza hemoglutinin molecule also  also suffers from conformational  instability  when the approach is taken to present  a headless aj molecule or a stock domain  only in the absence of the globular head  this approach is taken because the  globular head domain contains the major  antigenic sites for the molecule  and upon infection the immune system  targets this region generating  neutralizing antibodies  however these antibodies are often  strain specific  due to the process of antigenic drift  where the head in fact mutates over time  which causes the  vaccine to be updated on a yearly basis  so the idea of a headless h8 molecule is  to present the immune system  with the less immunogenic stock domain  given that it's primarily conserved year  to year and  elimination of the head uh would allow  focusing the immune responses on the  stockton  and it's been shown that the stock  domain itself  possess presents neutralizing epitopes  of the immune system  however attempts have been made to  recombinantly splice the head domain  from the molecule and or to  proteolytically remove the head domain  after it's folded and this results in a  loss of the stock  stock confirmation  so cauldre's approach is to apply the  additional stability  that a dityracy and crosslink imparts  to both of these problems in an effort  to lock in specific confirmations  and generate the most potent pre-fusion  specific  or conformationally intact immunogen  dietary bonds are present throughout  nature  and they're they're applied and found  in areas of proteins where a great deal  of structural rigidi